# apps/storefront — configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every one of these is read at BUILD time only;
# nothing here reaches the browser. Astro only inlines variables prefixed
# `PUBLIC_`, and none of these are — do not add a `PUBLIC_` alias for the
# token. Once `bun run build` finishes, the running container (`bun run
# serve`, `server/penyaji.mjs`) never reads an AWCMS_* variable again: a
# finished build never contacts awcms (issue #5).

# --- Site identity -----------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical absolute origin. Canonical links, Open Graph URLs, and the
# Product JSON-LD are all built from it. A wrong value does not fail the
# build; it publishes a site pointing every crawler and every share card
# somewhere else.
SITE_URL=https://mart.borneojek.com

# Optional. Falls back to a sensible default so `bun run dev` works with no
# `.env` at all.
SITE_NAME=Borneojek Mart
SITE_DESCRIPTION=Katalog produk borneojek-mart.

# Optional (issue #137, ADR-0018). Which page groups this build includes:
#   toko    — commerce + news (the default when unset; BjekMart's own shape)
#   berita  — news portal only
#   landing — company profile: home, static pages, contact
# Read at BUILD time by src/config/profil.ts; any other value fails the build.
# SITE_PROFILE=toko

# --- awcms content backend ---------------------------------------------------
# Origin of the awcms instance this build fetches the catalog from. No
# trailing slash needed; one is stripped.
AWCMS_API_URL=https://cms.example.com

# A BUILD-TIME, READ-ONLY credential. Used only while `astro build` runs to
# fetch the product and category list; never emitted into the output. Issue
# it with read-only access to the commerce module (products, categories) —
# nothing wider. A token in a static bundle would be a token published to
# every reader, which is exactly what NOT prefixing this `PUBLIC_` prevents.
AWCMS_API_TOKEN=awcmsm_replace-me

# OPTIONAL. How long one request to awcms may take before the build gives
# up, in milliseconds. Default 30000.
#
# Generous on purpose: this is a build-time deadline, not a request-time one,
# and a timeout tuned for a healthy request path would turn a slow build into
# a failed one. What it exists to catch is not slowness but SILENCE — a
# connection accepted and never answered — which without a deadline hangs the
# build until the CI job's own limit kills it, or forever on a workstation.
#
# A value that is not a positive number is REFUSED, not ignored — including
# `0`, which looks like "no limit" and would restore exactly that hang.
# AWCMS_API_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# OPTIONAL. This tenant's PUBLIC code on the awcms instance above — used only
# to read GET /theming/{tenantCode}/tokens.css (src/lib/awcms/theme.ts),
# which is how this build reads the CMS-configured --color-primary/
# --color-accent brand colors (see that file's docblock for why NOT
# GET /api/v1/theming). Unset is a normal, expected state — this build then
# uses BjekMart's own default palette (src/config/site.ts) rather than
# failing, the same way a missing AWCMS_TOKEN scope degrades site identity
# rather than failing the build.
# AWCMS_TENANT_CODE=bjekmart

# --- Anonymous commerce endpoints (issue #30, ADR-0007 revised) -------------
# The CMS's own public origin — the storefront stays 100% static (ADR-0002:
# no `prerender = false`, no runtime credential), but cart/checkout/order-
# tracking need somewhere for the BROWSER to POST to directly. The CMS
# resolves the tenant from the request `Origin` header and answers with CORS
# (`/api/v1/commerce/storefront/*` — see the #29⇄#30 endpoint contract),
# never a cookie, never a bearer token.
#
# Deliberately `PUBLIC_`-prefixed — this IS meant to reach the browser bundle
# (an origin is not a secret; see `src/lib/awcms/toko-origin.ts`). This is
# the ONE variable in this file that should be `PUBLIC_`. `AWCMS_API_TOKEN`
# above must NEVER gain a `PUBLIC_` alias — that would publish a build-time,
# read-only credential to every reader of this site.
#
# REQUIRED once issue #30 is deployed: unset (or malformed — must be a bare
# origin, no path/query/trailing slash) fails the BUILD, naming this
# variable, rather than shipping a checkout page that silently posts
# nowhere. May equal AWCMS_API_URL above (same CMS instance) or differ (a
# CDN/edge in front of the write path only) — this app makes no assumption
# either way.
PUBLIC_AWCMS_ORIGIN=https://cms.example.com

# OPTIONAL. Comma-separated Kemendagri province codes the checkout address
# step offers (`src/lib/awcms/wilayah-checkout.ts`), fetched at BUILD time
# into static `/index/wilayah-*.json` files — so a national ~90,000-village
# dataset is never baked into every deployment of this template. Defaults to
# every Kalimantan province ("61,62,63,64,65") — BjekMart's own service area.
# `PUBLIC_`-prefixed for consistency with the variable above even though no
# client script reads it directly (see that file's own docblock for why).
# PUBLIC_WILAYAH_PROVINSI=61,62,63,64,65

# --- Visitor analytics and the optional GA4 switch (issue #56) --------------
# The first-party visitor beacon (`src/scripts/analitik.ts`) is always
# mounted and needs NO variable of its own — it reuses `AWCMS_TENANT_CODE`
# above (baked into the page as a `data-*` attribute, never a second
# variable) and `PUBLIC_AWCMS_ORIGIN` above. See `apps/storefront/README.md`
# ("Visitor analytics and the optional GA4 switch") and
# `docs/deployment.md` ("The two switches") for the server-side
# `VISITOR_ANALYTICS_ENABLED` switch this beacon's data depends on —
# that variable lives in `apps/cms/.env.example`, not here.
#
# OPTIONAL. GA4's own Measurement ID (`G-…`). Unset, empty, or not shaped
# like one (`src/lib/ga.ts`) and this build ships with NO Google origin
# anywhere — no `gtag.js`, no widened CSP. `PUBLIC_`-prefixed deliberately: a
# GA4 Measurement ID is not a secret, it is broadcast in the page's own
# <script src> the instant this is set, the same way `PUBLIC_AWCMS_ORIGIN`
# above is public by construction.
# PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# --- Runtime (the only variables read AFTER the build) -----------------------
# `server/penyaji.mjs` reads these two and nothing else — it never reads an
# AWCMS_* variable, because a finished build never contacts awcms again.
#
# HOST defaults to 0.0.0.0 because the process normally runs inside a
# container behind a reverse proxy: one that listens on localhost only is
# unreachable from outside the container, which shows up as a health check
# that fails for no stated reason. On a workstation it means the preview is
# reachable from your whole network — set HOST=127.0.0.1 if that matters.
# PORT=8080
# HOST=0.0.0.0
